/* i18n.js — one panel, two languages.
 * (generated by `npm run i18n` — edit ui/i18n.en.json, ui/i18n.words.json and
 *  ui/i18n.connectors.json, then scripts/i18n-template.js if the logic changes.)
 *
 * The engine speaks Persian: job logs, stage labels and error banners are all
 * written in it, and the video it renders is Persian and right-to-left. This
 * file translates the *interface* into English when the reader's browser is not
 * Persian, without touching a single byte of the engine or of the captions.
 *
 * How it matches, in order:
 *   1. the whole text node or attribute against PHRASES — exact, so nothing is
 *      paraphrased by accident;
 *   2. otherwise word by word against WORDS — dynamic strings arrive already
 *      interpolated ("12 s, energy 60%"), so no static key can ever match them;
 *   3. function words (CONNECTORS) ride along, but only once a real term has
 *      matched, so a Persian sentence nobody translated stays Persian.
 *
 * Things that are *content*, not chrome, are left alone: input and textarea
 * values (the user's own copy), anything inside [data-no-i18n] (the beat
 * preview shows real card text), and code blocks (file paths are file paths).
 *
 * Locale comes from localStorage, then the browser; the choice is remembered.
 * Set `dir` on <html> so the whole layout mirrors with the language — the panel
 * is built on logical properties, so this is the only switch it needs.
 */
